\f0\fs34\b\cf1 Morphues Website - Code and Feature Guide\b0\cf0\fs22\par
\fs20 Prepared October 2026\par
\par
\b Purpose of this guide\b0\par
This guide explains the features and code changes made for the Morphues chat website during the conversation history, including responsive chat, profiles and friendships, themes, group chat, attachments, audio files, and voice notes. It describes how the main pieces work together and defines important programming terms. It is a feature-level guide to the work recorded in the project history, not a line-by-line explanation of every pre-existing line of the application.\par
\par
\b 1. How the application is organized\b0\par
The frontend is a React application. Pages display the screens; components are reusable parts of those screens; CSS files style them. React Router selects which page to show for a URL. The backend is an Express server in server.js. It verifies signed-in users, reads and writes PostgreSQL records, and emits live updates with Socket.IO.\par
The browser calls backend API routes with fetch(). The server checks the request, uses parameterized SQL queries through the PostgreSQL pool, and returns JSON or a file. The browser then updates React state and redraws the relevant part of the page.\par
\par
\b 2. Responsive chat and navigation\b0\par
The chat layout was adapted so it works on both small screens and desktop. On a narrow screen, the conversation list is shown when no conversation is selected; choosing a conversation shows the chat view. The message list scrolls inside the chat rather than forcing the entire mobile page to scroll. On larger screens, the design can show the conversation list and active chat together.\par
The chat list uses Friends and Groups tabs, a search field, and unread-message counts. The New chat control opens navigation to start a conversation or create a group. Group rows show their message activity. The mobile group-chat header includes a back button to return to chats.\par
Key files: src/pages/ChatPage.jsx, src/pages/GroupChatPage.jsx, src/pages/Layout.jsx, src/css/Chatpage.css, and src/css/Layout.css.\par
The responsive CSS uses media queries such as max-width: 768px. A media query applies styles only at matching viewport widths. Flexbox and CSS Grid arrange the controls and columns; min-width: 0 and overflow rules help long text fit without breaking the layout.\par
\par
\b 3. Light and dark appearance\b0\par
The Settings page has Light and Dark appearance choices. src/theme.js reads and saves the selection under the browser localStorage key dream-theme and applies it to the document root. src/css/Theme.css contains theme variables and light-mode overrides. Layout.jsx restores the chosen theme when the app opens and responds to theme changes. The saved choice remains after a page reload.\par
Important terms: localStorage is browser storage that persists for a site between page loads. A CSS custom property, written with a name beginning --, stores a reusable style value such as a surface or text color. data-theme is an HTML data attribute used by CSS selectors to choose a theme.\par
\par
\b 4. Sign-in, passwords, and token lifetime\b0\par
The login and signup pages include show/hide controls for password fields, so the user can check what they entered. These controls change whether the input is displayed as password text; they do not change or transmit the password by themselves.\par
The server signs users in with a JWT (JSON Web Token). The token is sent with authenticated API calls in the Authorization header. Login and signup tokens currently expire after one day. The one-day expiry was restored after a request to remove it was reconsidered. Expiration is a security limit; a user may need to sign in again when the token expires.\par
Key files: src/pages/LoginPage.jsx, src/pages/SignupPage.jsx, src/css/LoginPage.css, server.js, and authMiddleware.js.\par
\par
\b 5. Profiles, posts, statuses, and friend management\b0\par
The profile screen presents a user's identity and content with profile statistics and Posts and Status tabs. A signed-in user can edit their own photo and manage their own content. When viewing a friend's profile, the page is read-only for that person's account details; personal edit and delete controls are not shown. A friend can be messaged or removed, and the profile's friend count opens the friend list.\par
The server exposes profile and friend-list APIs. The other-user profile endpoint checks that the viewer is the profile owner or an accepted friend before returning that friend's profile content. Post and status deletion is restricted to the content owner. Status replies are sent through the direct-message system with status context in the message, so the recipient can see which status was replied to.\par
UserAvatarMenu is reused around avatars in the chat list, conversation header, feed posts and friend suggestions, inbox, and status list. Its menu can navigate to the selected user's profile or request opening that user's status. Statusbar reads the statusUser query parameter and opens the matching status when available.\par
The avatar photo upload uses the existing resizeImage helper to reduce image dimensions before sending the image data to the avatar API. The profile photo edit control uses an inline SVG camera icon.\par
Key files: src/pages/ProfilePage.jsx, src/css/Profile.css, src/pages/Feed.jsx, src/pages/Statusbar.jsx, src/css/StatusBar.css, src/components/UserAvatarMenu.jsx, src/css/UserAvatarMenu.css, src/resizeImage.jsx, and server.js.\par
Important terms: a route is a URL pattern mapped to a page; /profile/:userId uses a route parameter to select a person. A read-only view displays information without allowing changes. An endpoint is a backend URL that performs an API operation. Authorization determines what the signed-in user is allowed to see or change.\par
\par
\b 6. Finding people, friend requests, and groups\b0\par
The New Chat page has tabs for Everyone, Friends, and Discover, with search and loading, error, and empty states. Sending a friend request changes its button to a disabled Request sent state for the current page session. The friend request interface avoids letting the user send the same request repeatedly before the page state is refreshed.\par
The Create Group page lets a user search friends, select members, see the selected people, enter a group name, and review a preview before creating the group. The backend validates that added members are accepted friends. This is important because frontend restrictions alone cannot protect an API from an unauthorized request.\par
When a friend request is accepted, the backend creates or reuses a direct conversation and inserts a short welcome message. Chat lists refresh through Socket.IO events and periodic refreshes so both users see the new conversation.\par
Key files: src/pages/NewChat.jsx, src/css/NewChat.css, src/pages/CreateGroup.jsx, src/css/CreateGroup.css, src/pages/Layout.jsx, src/css/Layout.css, and server.js.\par
\par
\b 7. Attachments in direct and group chats\b0\par
The plus button in the composer opens an AttachmentPicker menu. The choices include Camera, Photo and video library, Audio, and Document. The document sheet provides a file picker and a photo/video picker. The hidden HTML file inputs invoke the operating system's file chooser; accept filters suggest the media type to choose. Camera capture is requested on supported mobile browsers.\par
Selected files are limited to 10 MB in the browser and checked again by the server. The client converts a file to a Base64 data URL for the JSON request. The server validates the incoming data, extracts its bytes, sanitizes its name, and saves it in PostgreSQL in the message_attachments table. That table is created when the server starts if it does not yet exist. Message creation and saving its attachment are wrapped in a database transaction so the message and file are committed together or rolled back together.\par
MessageAttachment automatically fetches attachment content when it appears in chat. It displays image and video previews, an audio play/pause player, and a separate download action. PDF documents are embedded for preview where supported by the browser; other document formats appear as named file cards with a separate download action. File content is fetched from an authenticated attachment endpoint rather than included in the normal message history response. Before returning a file, the server verifies the requester belongs to the direct conversation or group. The server returns the file name and MIME type and prevents shared caching.\par
Key files: src/components/AttachmentPicker.jsx, src/components/MessageAttachment.jsx, src/attachmentUtils.js, src/pages/ChatPage.jsx, src/pages/GroupChatPage.jsx, src/css/Chatpage.css, and server.js.\par
Important terms: Base64 is a text encoding for binary data; it increases file size during transfer, which is one reason attachments are kept small. BYTEA is PostgreSQL's binary data type. A database transaction groups operations so related writes succeed or fail together. MIME type identifies a file format, such as image/jpeg or audio/webm. A protected endpoint checks authentication and membership before returning file bytes.\par
\par
\b 8. Audio files and voice notes\b0\par
The Audio option opens the device's audio-file picker. Audio files and recorded voice notes are sent using the same attachment path as other files, so they use the same 10 MB limit, database table, membership checks, and message records.\par
VoiceNoteButton requests microphone access with navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia, then records the microphone stream with MediaRecorder. The user taps the microphone icon to begin and taps the stop control to finish and send the recording. The component selects a recording format supported by the browser when possible, builds a File from the recorded data chunks, and stops microphone tracks after recording. If permission is unavailable or recording fails, an error is shown. Browser support and a secure browser context (normally HTTPS, or localhost during development) are required for microphone access.\par
MessageAttachment fetches audio bytes and presents a custom play/pause button, progress slider, and time display. The audio element supplies playback; React state reflects whether it is playing, its current time, and its duration. The user can seek by changing the slider. If a browser blocks automatic playback, the user can press Play.\par
On screens at or below 640 CSS pixels, the Send text is visually hidden and an SVG send icon is shown instead. The button retains an accessible label through its text and icon presentation.\par
Key files: src/components/VoiceNoteButton.jsx, src/components/MessageAttachment.jsx, src/attachmentUtils.js, src/pages/ChatPage.jsx, src/pages/GroupChatPage.jsx, and src/css/Chatpage.css.\par
Important terms: MediaRecorder captures a MediaStream and produces recorded data chunks. A stream is a live flow of audio data from the microphone. A Blob is browser binary data; a File adds a name and type. An SVG is scalable vector artwork written as markup. aria-label provides a spoken label for assistive technology.\par
\par
\b 9. Real-time messaging and message controls\b0\par
Socket.IO keeps chat screens up to date without requiring a full page reload. The server broadcasts new messages to the relevant conversation or group room. The browser listens for those events and appends messages to React state. Existing message tools include reply, edit, delete, typing indicators, read receipts, and call-log cards. Status-reply messages receive a distinct contextual display.\par
Important terms: a WebSocket-style connection supports ongoing two-way messages between browser and server. Socket.IO manages that connection and named events. A room is a server-side group of sockets used to deliver an event to the relevant conversation members. React state is data that, when changed, causes the component to render again.\par
\par
\b 10. Backend safety and data rules\b0\par
Authenticated endpoints use authMiddleware and the JWT to identify the requester. SQL queries use parameters such as $1 and $2 rather than building SQL by joining user input into the query string. Friendship and group membership checks are performed server-side. Attachment names are sanitized before being returned as download names. The attachment endpoint is private and checks conversation or group membership.\par
Keep the one-day token expiry unless the sign-in and revocation model is deliberately redesigned. Do not store very large files in this PostgreSQL BYTEA approach; the current product limit is 10 MB per file. Larger files need a dedicated object-storage provider with access controls and upload/download URLs.\par
\par
\b 11. File map\b0\par
src/pages/ChatPage.jsx - Direct chat list and conversation, message sending, status callouts, attachment sending, and voice note integration.\par
src/pages/GroupChatPage.jsx - Group conversation, message sending, attachment sending, and voice note integration.\par
src/components/AttachmentPicker.jsx - Attachment menu, camera/media/file pickers, and document chooser.\par
src/components/MessageAttachment.jsx - Secure file loading UI and image, video, audio, and document presentation.\par
src/components/VoiceNoteButton.jsx - Microphone permission, recording lifecycle, timer, and voice-note send callback.\par
src/attachmentUtils.js - Shared attachment-size constant and FileReader helper.\par
src/css/Chatpage.css - Chat layout, responsive breakpoints, attachment menu and preview, voice-note controls, and mobile send icon.\par
src/pages/ProfilePage.jsx and src/css/Profile.css - Self and visitor profile display, friends list, friend actions, and profile photo control.\par
src/pages/NewChat.jsx and src/css/NewChat.css - Discovering users and sending friend requests.\par
src/pages/CreateGroup.jsx and src/css/CreateGroup.css - Group name and friend selection UI.\par
src/pages/Feed.jsx, src/pages/Statusbar.jsx, and status-related CSS - Posts, stories/statuses, status views, and replies.\par
src/pages/Layout.jsx and src/css/Layout.css - Shared application navigation and responsive layout.\par
src/pages/SettingsPage.jsx, src/theme.js, and src/css/Theme.css - Appearance controls and theme persistence.\par
src/pages/LoginPage.jsx, src/pages/SignupPage.jsx, and src/css/LoginPage.css - Account forms and password visibility controls.\par
server.js - Express API, authentication checks, PostgreSQL operations, attachment storage, and Socket.IO events.\par
README.md - High-level project description and feature overview.\par
\par
\b 12. Verification and running the project\b0\par
The frontend production build was run with npm.cmd run build and completed successfully after the attachment, audio-player, and voice-note changes. Editor diagnostics reported no errors in the files checked. The backend syntax was checked with node --check server.js, and git diff --check was run to find whitespace errors.\par
To run the frontend locally, install dependencies with npm install and start it with npm start. The backend uses npm run server and requires the project's environment variables and PostgreSQL database connection. Microphone recording usually needs HTTPS in a deployed environment. Backend API code changes must be deployed to the configured API host before remote users can use those server changes.\par
Build validation confirms the code compiles; it does not by itself prove that a live database connection, deployed API, microphone permission, or real device file picker works. Test those in the target environment with a signed-in test account.\par
\par
\b Glossary of important keywords\b0\par
API - A defined way for one program to request data or an action from another program.\par
Authorization header - HTTP request metadata carrying the user's access token.\par
Component - A reusable React UI unit, such as an attachment picker or profile card.\par
Endpoint - A specific backend URL and HTTP method that performs an operation.\par
Express - The Node.js web framework that defines server routes and middleware.\par
Hook - A React function such as useState, useEffect, or useRef that adds state, lifecycle behavior, or persistent references to a component.\par
JWT - A signed token used to identify an authenticated user on API requests.\par
Middleware - Server code that runs before a route, often to validate a token or parse a request.\par
PostgreSQL - The relational database used to store users, messages, groups, and attachments.\par
React Router - The library mapping browser paths to React pages and navigation.\par
REST - A common API style that uses HTTP methods such as GET, POST, PATCH, and DELETE.\par
Socket.IO - A library for real-time browser-server events used for chat updates.\par
State - Current component data; when React state changes, React updates the rendered UI.\par
SVG - Scalable Vector Graphics, used here for camera, microphone, play/pause, and send icons.\par
Validation - Checking incoming data against rules before accepting or storing it.\par
\par
\b End of guide\b0\par
\page
\b\fs30 Appendix A - Complete Source Code Listings\b0\fs22\par
The listings below are the complete current contents of the feature-related files in this workspace. These are included as code references; the files in the project remain the source of truth. Some files contain surrounding application code in addition to the requested feature changes. Line breaks and indentation are preserved.\par\par
\b README.md\b0\par
{\f1\fs15\cf2 \u-257?# Morphues\line
\line
Morphues is a sleek, real-time messaging and social app built for conversations that feel personal, fast, and alive. It blends private chats, group communities, and social discovery into one smooth experience.\line
\line
## What the website feels like\line
\line
Imagine a modern chat platform with:\line
\line
- a clean sidebar for inbox, groups, and requests\line
- quick access to direct messages and friend activity\line
- a polished dark-glass aesthetic with vibrant accents\line
- live messaging that feels instant and social\line
- community spaces where people can talk together in real time\line
\line
The app is designed to feel like a premium social hub where conversations move naturally from one friend or group to the next.\line
\line
## Highlights\line
\line
### Messaging experience\line
- Private one-on-one conversations\line
- Real-time sending and receiving of messages\line
- Photo, video, and document attachments in direct and group chats (up to 10 MB each)\line
- Audio attachments and microphone-recorded voice notes in direct and group chats\line
- Clean chat interface built for easy reading\line
\line
### Social features\line
- Friend requests and connection flow\line
- Group creation and community chat rooms\line
- A social dashboard that keeps conversations organized\line
\line
### Modern UI\line
- Minimal, stylish layout\line
- Responsive design for desktop and mobile-friendly viewing\line
- Soft gradients, modern typography, and a futuristic feel\line
\line
## App overview\line
\line
```text\line
+----------------------------------------------------+\line
| Morphues            Inbox   Groups   Requests      |\line
+----------------------------------------------------+\line
| Friends / Chats                  | Live Chat Thread |\line
| Alice                          | Hey, are you free  |\line
| Jordan                        | for tonight?       |\line
| Maya                          |                    |\line
| + New Chat                    | Reply...           |\line
+----------------------------------------------------+\line
```\line
\line
This gives the site a social-chat-app feel: organized on the left, active conversation in the center, and a modern polished interface throughout.\line
\line
## Tech stack\line
\line
- React\line
- Node.js\line
- Express\line
- Socket.IO\line
- PostgreSQL\line
- Custom real-time messaging backend\line
\line
## Getting started\line
\line
1. Install dependencies:\line
\line
```bash\line
npm install\line
```\line
\line
2. Start the app in development mode:\line
\line
```bash\line
npm start\line
```\line
\line
3. Open the app in your browser at:\line
\line
```text\line
http://localhost:3000\line
```\line
\line
## Project purpose\line
\line
Morphues is more than a chat app. It is built to feel like a social space where people can connect, create communities, and keep conversations flowing naturally in real time.\line
\line
## License\line
\line
This project is for personal and educational use unless otherwise specified by the project owner.\line
# Morphues}\par\par
\b server.js\b0\par
{\f1\fs15\cf2 require('dotenv').config();\line
const express = require('express');\line
const cors = require('cors');\line
const pool = require('./db');\line
const bcrypt = require('bcrypt');\line
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');\line
const http = require('http');\line
const \{ Server \} = require('socket.io');\line
const authMiddleware = require('./authMiddleware');\line
\line
const app = express();\line
app.use(cors());\line
app.use(express.json(\{ limit: '15mb' \}));\line
\line
const MAX_ATTACHMENT_SIZE = 10 * 1024 * 1024;\line
\line
function parseAttachment(value) \{\line
  if (!value || typeof value !== 'object' || typeof value.data !== 'string') \{\line
    throw new Error('Invalid attachment.');\line
  \}\line
\line
  const dataUrl = /^data:([^;,]+);base64,([A-Za-z0-9+/]*=\{0,2\})$/.exec(value.data);\line
  if (!dataUrl) throw new Error('Invalid attachment data.');\line
\line
  const buffer = Buffer.from(dataUrl[2], 'base64');\line
  if (buffer.toString('base64') !== dataUrl[2]) throw new Error('Invalid attachment data.');\line
  if (buffer.length > MAX_ATTACHMENT_SIZE) throw new Error('Attachments must be 10 MB or smaller.');\line
\line
  const fileName = String(value.file_name || 'attachment')\line
    .replace(/[\\\\/\\u0000-\\u001f\\u007f]/g, '_')\line
    .trim()\line
    .slice(0, 180) || 'attachment';\line
  const mimeType = /^[\\w.+-]+\\/[\\w.+-]+$/.test(dataUrl[1])\line
    ? dataUrl[1].toLowerCase()\line
    : 'application/octet-stream';\line
\line
  return \{ fileName, mimeType, buffer \};\line
\}\line
\line
async function saveAttachment(messageId, attachment, db = pool) \{\line
  if (!attachment) return null;\line
  const result = await db.query(\line
    `INSERT INTO message_attachments (message_id, file_name, mime_type, file_size, data)\line
     VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5)\line
     RETURNING file_name, mime_type, file_size`,\line
    [messageId, attachment.fileName, attachment.mimeType, attachment.buffer.length, attachment.buffer]\line
  );\line
  const saved = result.rows[0];\line
  return \{\line
    file_name: saved.file_name,\line
    mime_type: saved.mime_type,\line
    file_size: saved.file_size,\line
  \};\line
\}\line
\line
async function insertMessage(query, values, attachment) \{\line
  if (!attachment) \{\line
    return \{ result: await pool.query(query, values), savedAttachment: null \};\line
  \}\line
\line
  const client = await pool.connect();\line
  try \{\line
    await client.query('BEGIN');\line
    const result = await client.query(query, values);\line
    const savedAttachment = await saveAttachment(result.rows[0].id, attachment, client);\line
    await client.query('COMMIT');\line
    return \{ result, savedAttachment \};\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    try \{\line
      await client.query('ROLLBACK');\line
    \} catch (rollbackError) \{\line
      console.error('Message attachment rollback error:', rollbackError);\line
    \}\line
    throw err;\line
  \} finally \{\line
    client.release();\line
  \}\line
\}\line
\line
function getAttachmentMetadata(row) \{\line
  if (!row.attachment_name) return null;\line
  return \{\line
    file_name: row.attachment_name,\line
    mime_type: row.attachment_mime_type,\line
    file_size: row.attachment_file_size,\line
  \};\line
\}\line
\line
function orderUserIds(idA, idB) \{\line
  return idA < idB ? [idA, idB] : [idB, idA];\line
\}\line
\line
// --- AUTH ---\line
\line
app.post('/api/auth/login', async (req, res) => \{\line
  const \{ email, password \} = req.body;\line
  if (!email || !password) \{\line
    return res.status(400).json(\{ message: "Email and password are required." \});\line
  \}\line
  try \{\line
    const result = await pool.query(`SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = $1`, [email]);\line
    const user = result.rows[0];\line
    if (!user) \{\line
      return res.status(401).json(\{ message: "Invalid email or password." \});\line
    \}\line
    const passwordMatch = await bcrypt.compare(password, user.password_hash);\line
    if (!passwordMatch) \{\line
      return res.status(401).json(\{ message: "Invalid email or password." \});\line
    \}\line
    const token = jwt.sign(\{ userId: user.id \}, process.env.JWT_SECRET, \{ expiresIn: '1d' \});\line
    return res.json(\{\line
      token,\line
      user: \{ id: user.id, username: user.username, email: user.email ,avatar:user.avatar\}\line
    \});\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Login error:', err);\line
    return res.status(500).json(\{ message: "Internal server error." \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
\line
app.post('/api/auth/signup', async (req, res) => \{\line
  const \{ username, email, password \} = req.body;\line
  if (!username || !email || !password) \{\line
    return res.status(400).json(\{ message: 'Username, email, and password are required.' \});\line
  \}\line
  try \{\line
    const existing = await pool.query('SELECT id FROM users WHERE email = $1', [email]);\line
    if (existing.rows.length > 0) \{\line
      return res.status(409).json(\{ message: 'An account with that email already exists.' \});\line
    \}\line
    const passwordHash = await bcrypt.hash(password, 10);\line
    const result = await pool.query(\line
      `INSERT INTO users (username, email, password_hash,avatar)\line
       VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4)\line
       RETURNING id, username, email, avatar`,\line
      [username, email, passwordHash, null]\line
    );\line
    const user = result.rows[0];\line
    const token = jwt.sign(\{ userId: user.id \}, process.env.JWT_SECRET, \{ expiresIn: '1d' \});\line
    res.status(201).json(\{ token, user \});\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Signup error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
// --Backend \line
\line
// --- USERS ---\line
\line
app.get('/api/users', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  try \{\line
    const result = await pool.query(\line
      'SELECT id, username, avatar FROM users WHERE id != $1',\line
      [req.userId]\line
    );\line
    res.json(result.rows);\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Get users error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
\line
app.get('/api/users/:userId/profile', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  const profileUserId = Number(req.params.userId);\line
  if (!Number.isInteger(profileUserId) || profileUserId <= 0) \{\line
    return res.status(400).json(\{ message: 'Invalid user ID.' \});\line
  \}\line
\line
  try \{\line
    if (profileUserId !== Number(req.userId)) \{\line
      const friendship = await pool.query(\line
        `SELECT 1 FROM friendships\line
         WHERE ((requester_id = $1 AND addressee_id = $2) OR (requester_id = $2 AND addressee_id = $1))\line
           AND status = 'accepted'`,\line
        [req.userId, profileUserId]\line
      );\line
      if (friendship.rows.length === 0) \{\line
        return res.status(403).json(\{ message: 'You can only view a friend\u8217?s profile.' \});\line
      \}\line
    \}\line
\line
    const [profileResult, postsResult, statusesResult, friendsResult] = await Promise.all([\line
      pool.query(\line
        'SELECT id, username, avatar FROM users WHERE id = $1',\line
        [profileUserId]\line
      ),\line
      pool.query(\line
        `SELECT p.id, p.caption, p.image_url, p.created_at,\line
                u.id AS user_id, u.username, u.avatar,\line
                COUNT(DISTINCT pl.user_id)::int AS like_count,\line
                COUNT(DISTINCT pc.id)::int AS comment_count,\line
                COALESCE(BOOL_OR(pl.user_id = $1), FALSE) AS liked_by_me\line
         FROM posts p\line
         JOIN users u ON u.id = p.user_id\line
         LEFT JOIN post_likes pl ON pl.post_id = p.id\line
         LEFT JOIN post_comments pc ON pc.post_id = p.id\line
         WHERE p.user_id = $2\line
         GROUP BY p.id, u.id\line
         ORDER BY p.created_at DESC`,\line
        [req.userId, profileUserId]\line
      ),\line
      pool.query(\line
        `SELECT s.id, s.content, s.image_url, s.background_color, s.created_at,\line
                u.id AS user_id, u.username, u.avatar,\line
                EXISTS (\line
                  SELECT 1 FROM status_views sv\line
                  WHERE sv.status_id = s.id AND sv.viewer_id = $1\line
                ) AS viewed_by_me\line
         FROM statuses s\line
         JOIN users u ON u.id = s.user_id\line
         WHERE s.user_id = $2 AND s.created_at > NOW() - INTERVAL '24 hours'\line
         ORDER BY s.created_at DESC`,\line
        [req.userId, profileUserId]\line
      ),\line
      pool.query(\line
        `SELECT u.id, u.username, u.avatar\line
         FROM friendships f\line
         JOIN users u ON u.id = CASE WHEN f.requester_id = $1 THEN f.addressee_id ELSE f.requester_id END\line
         WHERE (f.requester_id = $1 OR f.addressee_id = $1) AND f.status = 'accepted'\line
         ORDER BY u.username`,\line
        [profileUserId]\line
      ),\line
    ]);\line
\line
    if (profileResult.rows.length === 0) \{\line
      return res.status(404).json(\{ message: 'User not found.' \});\line
    \}\line
\line
    res.json(\{\line
      user: profileResult.rows[0],\line
      posts: postsResult.rows,\line
      statuses: statusesResult.rows,\line
      friends: friendsResult.rows,\line
      friendCount: friendsResult.rows.length,\line
    \});\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Get user profile error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
\line
app.get('/api/users/:userId/friends', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  const profileUserId = Number(req.params.userId);\line
  if (!Number.isInteger(profileUserId) || profileUserId <= 0) \{\line
    return res.status(400).json(\{ message: 'Invalid user ID.' \});\line
  \}\line
\line
  try \{\line
    if (profileUserId !== Number(req.userId)) \{\line
      const friendship = await pool.query(\line
        `SELECT 1 FROM friendships\line
         WHERE ((requester_id = $1 AND addressee_id = $2) OR (requester_id = $2 AND addressee_id = $1))\line
           AND status = 'accepted'`,\line
        [req.userId, profileUserId]\line
      );\line
      if (friendship.rows.length === 0) \{\line
        return res.status(403).json(\{ message: 'You can only view a friend\u8217?s friends.' \});\line
      \}\line
    \}\line
\line
    const friends = await pool.query(\line
      `SELECT u.id, u.username, u.avatar\line
       FROM friendships f\line
       JOIN users u ON u.id = CASE WHEN f.requester_id = $1 THEN f.addressee_id ELSE f.requester_id END\line
       WHERE (f.requester_id = $1 OR f.addressee_id = $1) AND f.status = 'accepted'\line
       ORDER BY u.username`,\line
      [profileUserId]\line
    );\line
    res.json(friends.rows);\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Get user friends error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
\line
// --- CONVERSATIONS ---\line
\line
app.post('/api/conversations', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  const otherUserId = Number(req.body.otherUserId);\line
  if (!otherUserId) \{\line
    return res.status(400).json(\{ message: 'otherUserId is required.' \});\line
  \}\line
  if (otherUserId === req.userId) \{\line
    return res.status(400).json(\{ message: "You can't message yourself." \});\line
  \}\line
\line
  const [userOneId, userTwoId] = orderUserIds(req.userId, otherUserId);\line
\line
  try \{\line
    // only friends can start a conversation\line
    const friendship = await pool.query(\line
      `SELECT 1 FROM friendships\line
       WHERE ((requester_id = $1 AND addressee_id = $2) OR (requester_id = $2 AND addressee_id = $1))\line
         AND status = 'accepted'`,\line
      [req.userId, otherUserId]\line
    );\line
    if (friendship.rows.length === 0) \{\line
      return res.status(403).json(\{ message: 'You must be friends to start a conversation.' \});\line
    \}\line
\line
    // reuse the conversation if it already exists\line
    const existing = await pool.query(\line
      `SELECT * FROM conversations WHERE user_one_id = $1 AND user_two_id = $2 LIMIT 1`,\line
      [userOneId, userTwoId]\line
    );\line
    if (existing.rows.length > 0) \{\line
      return res.status(200).json(existing.rows[0]);\line
    \}\line
\line
    try \{\line
      const created = await pool.query(\line
        `INSERT INTO conversations (user_one_id, user_two_id) VALUES ($1, $2) RETURNING *`,\line
        [userOneId, userTwoId]\line
      );\line
      return res.status(201).json(created.rows[0]);\line
    \} catch (insertError) \{\line
      // 23505 = unique violation: another request created it a moment ago\line
      if (insertError.code !== '23505') throw insertError;\line
      const again = await pool.query(\line
        `SELECT * FROM conversations WHERE user_one_id = $1 AND user_two_id = $2 LIMIT 1`,\line
        [userOneId, userTwoId]\line
      );\line
      return res.status(200).json(again.rows[0]);\line
    \}\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Conversation error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
\line
app.get('/api/conversations', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  try \{\line
    const result = await pool.query(\line
      `SELECT \line
         c.id AS conversation_id,\line
         CASE WHEN c.user_one_id = $1 THEN u2.username ELSE u1.username END AS other_username,\line
         CASE WHEN c.user_one_id = $1 THEN c.user_two_id ELSE c.user_one_id END AS other_user_id,\line
         CASE WHEN c.user_one_id = $1 THEN u2.avatar ELSE u1.avatar END AS other_user_avatar,\line
         m.content AS last_message,\line
         m.created_at AS last_message_at,\line
         COALESCE(m.user_id != $1 AND m.read_at IS NULL, FALSE) AS last_message_unread,\line
         COALESCE(unread.unread_count, 0)::int AS unread_count\line
       FROM conversations c\line
       JOIN users u1 ON c.user_one_id = u1.id\line
       JOIN users u2 ON c.user_two_id = u2.id\line
       LEFT JOIN LATERAL (\line
         SELECT content, created_at, user_id, read_at\line
         FROM messages\line
         WHERE messages.conversation_id = c.id\line
         ORDER BY created_at DESC\line
         LIMIT 1\line
       ) m ON true\line
       LEFT JOIN LATERAL (\line
         SELECT COUNT(*) AS unread_count\line
         FROM messages\line
         WHERE messages.conversation_id = c.id\line
           AND messages.user_id != $1\line
           AND messages.read_at IS NULL\line
       ) unread ON true\line
       WHERE c.user_one_id = $1 OR c.user_two_id = $1\line
       ORDER BY m.created_at DESC NULLS LAST`,\line
      [req.userId]\line
    );\line
    res.json(result.rows);\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Get conversations error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
// Send a friend request\line
app.post('/api/friends/request', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  const \{ addresseeId \} = req.body;\line
  if (!addresseeId) return res.status(400).json(\{ message: 'addresseeId is required.' \});\line
  if (addresseeId === req.userId) return res.status(400).json(\{ message: "You can't friend yourself." \});\line
\line
  try \{\line
    const existing = await pool.query(\line
      `SELECT * FROM friendships\line
       WHERE (requester_id = $1 AND addressee_id = $2)\line
          OR (requester_id = $2 AND addressee_id = $1)`,\line
      [req.userId, addresseeId]\line
    );\line
    if (existing.rows.length > 0) \{\line
      return res.status(409).json(\{ message: 'A friend request already exists.', status: existing.rows[0].status \});\line
    \}\line
\line
    const result = await pool.query(\line
      `INSERT INTO friendships (requester_id, addressee_id, status)\line
       VALUES ($1, $2, 'pending') RETURNING *`,\line
      [req.userId, addresseeId]\line
    );\line
\line
    const notif = await pool.query(\line
      `INSERT INTO notifications (user_id, actor_id, type)\line
       VALUES ($1, $2, 'friend_request') RETURNING *`,\line
      [addresseeId, req.userId]\line
    );\line
\line
    io.to(`user:$\{addresseeId\}`).emit('newNotification', notif.rows[0]);\line
    io.to(`user:$\{addresseeId\}`).emit('friendRequestReceived', result.rows[0]); // keep this too, Requests page still needs it\line
\line
    res.status(201).json(result.rows[0]);\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Friend request error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
\line
// Respond to a friend request (accept or decline)\line
app.patch('/api/friends/:friendshipId', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  const \{ friendshipId \} = req.params;\line
  const \{ status \} = req.body; // 'accepted' or 'declined'\line
\line
  if (!['accepted', 'declined'].includes(status)) \{\line
    return res.status(400).json(\{ message: 'Status must be accepted or declined.' \});\line
  \}\line
\line
  const client = await pool.connect();\line
  let acceptedConversationMessage = null;\line
  let acceptedConversationId = null;\line
  let requesterId = null;\line
\line
  try \{\line
    await client.query('BEGIN');\line
\line
    // only the addressee can respond to a request sent to them\line
    const result = await client.query(\line
      `UPDATE friendships SET status = $1\line
       WHERE id = $2 AND addressee_id = $3 AND status = 'pending'\line
       RETURNING *`,\line
      [status, friendshipId, req.userId]\line
    );\line
\line
    if (result.rows.length === 0) \{\line
      await client.query('ROLLBACK');\line
      return res.status(403).json(\{ message: 'Request not found or already handled.' \});\line
    \}\line
\line
    const updated = result.rows[0];\line
    requesterId = updated.requester_id;\line
\line
    if (status === 'accepted') \{\line
      const [userOneId, userTwoId] = orderUserIds(Number(req.userId), Number(requesterId));\line
      const insertedConversation = await client.query(\line
        `INSERT INTO conversations (user_one_id, user_two_id)\line
         VALUES ($1, $2)\line
         ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING\line
         RETURNING id`,\line
        [userOneId, userTwoId]\line
      );\line
      const conversationId = insertedConversation.rows[0]?.id\line
        ?? (await client.query(\line
          `SELECT id FROM conversations WHERE user_one_id = $1 AND user_two_id = $2`,\line
          [userOneId, userTwoId]\line
        )).rows[0]?.id;\line
\line
      if (!conversationId) \{\line
        throw new Error('Failed to create or find the new friends conversation.');\line
      \}\line
\line
      const accepterResult = await client.query(\line
        'SELECT username, avatar FROM users WHERE id = $1',\line
        [req.userId]\line
      );\line
      const messageContent = "You're now friends. Say hello!";\line
      const messageResult = await client.query(\line
        `INSERT INTO messages (content, user_id, conversation_id)\line
         VALUES ($1, $2, $3)\line
         RETURNING id, content, created_at, reply_to_id`,\line
        [messageContent, req.userId, conversationId]\line
      );\line
\line
      acceptedConversationId = conversationId;\line
      acceptedConversationMessage = \{\line
        ...messageResult.rows[0],\line
        username: accepterResult.rows[0].username,\line
        avatar: accepterResult.rows[0].avatar,\line
        user_id: req.userId,\line
        read_at: null,\line
        conversationId: Number(conversationId),\line
      \};\line
    \}\line
\line
    await client.query('COMMIT');\line
    io.to(`user:$\{requesterId\}`).emit('friendRequestResponded', updated);\line
\line
    if (status === 'accepted') \{\line
      io.to(`conversation:$\{acceptedConversationId\}`).emit('newMessage', acceptedConversationMessage);\line
      io.to(`user:$\{req.userId\}`).emit('conversationCreated');\line
      io.to(`user:$\{requesterId\}`).emit('conversationCreated');\line
      io.to(`user:$\{requesterId\}`).emit('unreadMessagesChanged');\line
    \}\line
\line
    res.json(updated);\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    try \{\line
      await client.query('ROLLBACK');\line
    \} catch (rollbackError) \{\line
      console.error('Friend request rollback error:', rollbackError);\line
    \}\line
    console.error('Respond to request error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \} finally \{\line
    client.release();\line
  \}\line
\});\line
\line
// List my friends (accepted only) and anyone I could still friend\line
app.get('/api/friends', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  try \{\line
    const friends = await pool.query(\line
      `SELECT u.id, u.username, u.avatar  \line
       FROM friendships f\line
       JOIN users u ON u.id = CASE WHEN f.requester_id = $1 THEN f.addressee_id ELSE f.requester_id END\line
       WHERE (f.requester_id = $1 OR f.addressee_id = $1) AND f.status = 'accepted'`,\line
      [req.userId]\line
    );\line
    res.json(friends.rows);\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Get friends error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
\line
app.delete('/api/friends/:friendId', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  const friendId = Number(req.params.friendId);\line
  if (!Number.isInteger(friendId) || friendId <= 0 || friendId === Number(req.userId)) \{\line
    return res.status(400).json(\{ message: 'Invalid friend ID.' \});\line
  \}\line
\line
  try \{\line
    const result = await pool.query(\line
      `DELETE FROM friendships\line
       WHERE ((requester_id = $1 AND addressee_id = $2) OR (requester_id = $2 AND addressee_id = $1))\line
         AND status = 'accepted'\line
       RETURNING id`,\line
      [req.userId, friendId]\line
    );\line
    if (result.rowCount === 0) \{\line
      return res.status(404).json(\{ message: 'Friendship not found.' \});\line
    \}\line
    res.json(\{ message: 'Friend removed.' \});\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Remove friend error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
\line
// List pending requests sent TO me\line
app.get('/api/friends/requests', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  try \{\line
    const result = await pool.query(\line
      `SELECT f.id AS friendship_id, u.id AS requester_id, u.username, u.avatar\line
       FROM friendships f\line
       JOIN users u ON u.id = f.requester_id\line
       WHERE f.addressee_id = $1 AND f.status = 'pending'`,\line
      [req.userId]\line
    );\line
    res.json(result.rows);\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Get requests error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
\line
// --- MESSAGES (scoped to a conversation) ---\line
\line
app.post('/api/conversations/:conversationId/messages', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  const \{ conversationId \} = req.params;\line
  const \{ content, replyToId \} = req.body;\line
  let messageContent = content;\line
  let attachment = null;\line
  try \{\line
    if (req.body.attachment !== undefined) attachment = parseAttachment(req.body.attachment);\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    return res.status(400).json(\{ message: err.message \});\line
  \}\line
  if ((!content || !content.trim()) && !attachment) \{\line
    return res.status(400).json(\{ message: 'Message cannot be empty.' \});\line
  \}\line
  if (attachment && (!messageContent || !messageContent.trim())) \{\line
    messageContent = `\u-10179? $\{attachment.fileName\}`;\line
  \}\line
\line
  try \{\line
    if (attachment) \{\line
      const membership = await pool.query(\line
        `SELECT 1 FROM conversations\line
         WHERE id = $1 AND (user_one_id = $2 OR user_two_id = $2)`,\line
        [conversationId, req.userId]\line
      );\line
      if (membership.rows.length === 0) \{\line
        return res.status(403).json(\{ message: 'You are not a member of this conversation.' \});\line
      \}\line
    \}\line
\line
    const \{ result, savedAttachment \} = await insertMessage(\line
      `WITH inserted AS (\line
         INSERT INTO messages (content, user_id, conversation_id, reply_to_id)\line
         VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4)\line
         RETURNING id, content, created_at, reply_to_id\line
       )\line
       SELECT inserted.*, r.content AS reply_content, ru.username AS reply_username\line
       FROM inserted\line
       LEFT JOIN messages r ON inserted.reply_to_id = r.id\line
       LEFT JOIN users ru ON r.user_id = ru.id`,\line
      [messageContent, req.userId, conversationId, replyToId || null],\line
      attachment\line
    );\line
\line
    const userResult = await pool.query('SELECT username, avatar FROM users WHERE id = $1', [req.userId]);\line
    const fullMessage = \{\line
      ...result.rows[0],\line
      attachment: savedAttachment,\line
      username: userResult.rows[0].username,\line
      avatar: userResult.rows[0].avatar,\line
      user_id: req.userId,\line
      read_at: null,\line
      conversationId: Number(conversationId),\line
    \};\line
\line
    io.to(`conversation:$\{conversationId\}`).emit('newMessage', fullMessage);\line
\line
    // Tell the OTHER person's browser to refresh their unread badge.\line
    const convo = await pool.query(\line
      'SELECT user_one_id, user_two_id FROM conversations WHERE id = $1',\line
      [conversationId]\line
    );\line
    if (convo.rows.length > 0) \{\line
      const \{ user_one_id, user_two_id \} = convo.rows[0];\line
      const recipientId = user_one_id === req.userId ? user_two_id : user_one_id;\line
      io.to(`user:$\{recipientId\}`).emit('unreadMessagesChanged');\line
    \}\line
\line
    res.status(201).json(fullMessage);\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Post message error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
\line
app.get('/api/conversations/:conversationId/messages', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  const \{ conversationId \} = req.params;\line
  try \{\line
    const result = await pool.query(\line
      `SELECT \line
         m.id, m.content, m.created_at, m.read_at, m.edited_at, m.user_id, m.reply_to_id,\line
         u.username,\line
         u.avatar AS user_avatar,     \line
         r.content AS reply_content,\line
         ru.username AS reply_username,\line
         a.file_name AS attachment_name,\line
         a.mime_type AS attachment_mime_type,\line
         a.file_size AS attachment_file_size\line
       FROM messages m\line
       JOIN users u ON m.user_id = u.id\line
       LEFT JOIN messages r ON m.reply_to_id = r.id\line
       LEFT JOIN users ru ON r.user_id = ru.id\line
       LEFT JOIN message_attachments a ON a.message_id = m.id\line
       WHERE m.conversation_id = $1\line
       ORDER BY m.created_at ASC`,\line
      [conversationId]\line
    );\line
    res.json(result.rows.map((row) => (\{ ...row, attachment: getAttachmentMetadata(row) \})));\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Get messages error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
\line
app.get('/api/messages/:messageId/attachment', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  try \{\line
    const result = await pool.query(\line
      `SELECT a.file_name, a.mime_type, a.file_size, a.data\line
       FROM message_attachments a\line
       JOIN messages m ON m.id = a.message_id\line
       WHERE m.id = $1\line
         AND (\line
           (m.conversation_id IS NOT NULL AND EXISTS (\line
             SELECT 1 FROM conversations c\line
             WHERE c.id = m.conversation_id\line
               AND (c.user_one_id = $2 OR c.user_two_id = $2)\line
           ))\line
           OR (m.group_id IS NOT NULL AND EXISTS (\line
             SELECT 1 FROM group_members gm\line
             WHERE gm.group_id = m.group_id AND gm.user_id = $2\line
           ))\line
         )`,\line
      [req.params.messageId, req.userId]\line
    );\line
    if (result.rows.length === 0) \{\line
      return res.status(404).json(\{ message: 'Attachment not found.' \});\line
    \}\line
\line
    const attachment = result.rows[0];\line
    const fallbackName = attachment.file_name.replace(/[^\\x20-\\x7E]|["\\\\]/g, '_');\line
    res.set(\{\line
      'Content-Type': attachment.mime_type,\line
      'Content-Length': attachment.file_size,\line
      'Content-Disposition': `attachment; filename="$\{fallbackName\}"; filename*=UTF-8''$\{encodeURIComponent(attachment.file_name)\}`,\line
      'X-Content-Type-Options': 'nosniff',\line
      'Cache-Control': 'private, no-store',\line
    \});\line
    res.send(attachment.data);\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Get message attachment error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
// Total unread DMs for the Messages badge\line
app.get('/api/messages/unread-count', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  try \{\line
    const result = await pool.query(\line
      `SELECT COUNT(*)::int AS count\line
       FROM messages m\line
       JOIN conversations c ON m.conversation_id = c.id\line
       WHERE (c.user_one_id = $1 OR c.user_two_id = $1)\line
         AND m.user_id != $1\line
         AND m.read_at IS NULL`,\line
      [req.userId]\line
    );\line
    res.json(\{ count: result.rows[0].count \});\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Unread count error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
// Edit a message \u8212? only the sender can edit their own message\line
app.patch('/api/messages/:messageId', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  const \{ messageId \} = req.params;\line
  const \{ content \} = req.body;\line
\line
  if (!content || !content.trim()) \{\line
    return res.status(400).json(\{ message: 'Message cannot be empty.' \});\line
  \}\line
\line
  try \{\line
    const result = await pool.query(\line
      `UPDATE messages\line
       SET content = $1, edited_at = NOW()\line
       WHERE id = $2 AND user_id = $3\line
       RETURNING id, content, edited_at, conversation_id`,\line
      [content, messageId, req.userId]\line
    );\line
\line
    if (result.rows.length === 0) \{\line
      return res.status(403).json(\{ message: 'You can only edit your own messages.' \});\line
    \}\line
\line
    const updated = result.rows[0];\line
    io.to(`conversation:$\{updated.conversation_id\}`).emit('messageEdited', updated);\line
\line
    res.json(updated);\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Edit message error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
\line
// Delete a message \u8212? only the sender can delete their own message\line
app.delete('/api/messages/:messageId', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  const \{ messageId \} = req.params;\line
\line
  try \{\line
    const result = await pool.query(\line
      `DELETE FROM messages WHERE id = $1 AND user_id = $2 RETURNING id, conversation_id`,\line
      [messageId, req.userId]\line
    );\line
\line
    if (result.rows.length === 0) \{\line
      return res.status(403).json(\{ message: 'You can only delete your own messages.' \});\line
    \}\line
\line
    const deleted = result.rows[0];\line
    io.to(`conversation:$\{deleted.conversation_id\}`).emit('messageDeleted', \{\line
      id: deleted.id,\line
      conversationId: deleted.conversation_id,\line
    \});\line
\line
    res.status(200).json(\{ message: 'Message deleted.' \});\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Delete message error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
// --- READ RECEIPTS ---\line
\line
app.patch('/api/conversations/:conversationId/read', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  const \{ conversationId \} = req.params;\line
  try \{\line
    await pool.query(\line
      `UPDATE messages\line
       SET read_at = NOW()\line
       WHERE conversation_id = $1\line
         AND user_id != $2\line
         AND read_at IS NULL`,\line
      [conversationId, req.userId]\line
    );\line
\line
    io.to(`conversation:$\{conversationId\}`).emit('messagesRead', \{\line
      conversationId: Number(conversationId),\line
      readerId: req.userId,\line
    \});\line
\line
    io.to(`user:$\{req.userId\}`).emit('unreadMessagesChanged');\line
\line
    res.status(200).json(\{ message: 'Marked as read.' \});\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Mark read error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
//Create groups\line
app.post('/api/groups',authMiddleware,async (req,res)=>\{\line
  const \{name,memberIds\}=req.body;\line
  if(!name || !name.trim())\{\line
    return res.status(400).json(\{message:'Groups name is required.'\})\line
  \}\line
  try\{\line
    const group = await pool.query(\line
      `INSERT INTO groups (name,created_by) VALUES ($1,$2) RETURNING *`,\line
      [name,req.userId]\line
    )\line
    const groupId = group.rows[0].id;\line
    //creator joins automatically\line
    await pool.query(\line
      `INSERT INTO group_members (group_id,user_id) VALUES ($1,$2)`,\line
      [groupId,req.userId]\line
    )\line
    //add initial members, but only if they are actually friends \line
    if(Array.isArray(memberIds))\{\line
      for (const memberId of memberIds)\{\line
        const friendship = await pool.query(\line
          `SELECT * FROM friendships\line
           WHERE ((requester_id = $1 AND addressee_id = $2) OR (requester_id = $2 AND addressee_id = $1))\line
             AND status = 'accepted'`,\line
          [req.userId, memberId]\line
        );\line
        if(friendship.rows.length>0)\{\line
          await pool.query(\line
            `INSERT INTO group_members (group_id,user_id) VALUES ($1,$2)\line
            ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`,\line
            [groupId,memberId]\line
          )\line
        \}\line
      \}\line
  \}\line
  res.status(201).json(group.rows[0]);\line
\line
\}catch(err)\{\line
console.error('Create group error:',err);\line
res.status(500).json(\{message:'Internal server error.'\});\line
  \}\line
\})\line
//listing groups\line
app.get('/api/groups', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  try\{\line
    const result = await pool.query(\line
      `SELECT g.id, g.name, g.created_by,\line
              COUNT(m.id)::int AS message_count,\line
              COUNT(m.id) FILTER (\line
                WHERE m.user_id != $1 AND m.read_at IS NULL\line
              )::int AS unread_count\line
       FROM groups g\line
       JOIN group_members gm ON g.id = gm.group_id\line
       LEFT JOIN messages m ON m.group_id = g.id\line
       WHERE gm.user_id = $1\line
       GROUP BY g.id, g.name, g.created_by\line
       ORDER BY g.name ASC`,\line
      [req.userId]\line
    );\line
    res.json(result.rows);\line
  \}\line
  catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('List groups error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\})\line
//sending group messages\line
app.post('/api/groups/:groupId/messages', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  const \{ groupId \} = req.params;\line
  const \{ content \} = req.body;\line
  let messageContent = content;\line
  let attachment = null;\line
  try \{\line
    if (req.body.attachment !== undefined) attachment = parseAttachment(req.body.attachment);\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    return res.status(400).json(\{ message: err.message \});\line
  \}\line
  if ((!content || !content.trim()) && !attachment) \{\line
    return res.status(400).json(\{ message: 'Message cannot be empty.' \});\line
  \}\line
  if (attachment && (!messageContent || !messageContent.trim())) \{\line
    messageContent = `\u-10179? $\{attachment.fileName\}`;\line
  \}\line
\line
  try \{\line
    // confirm the sender is actually a member\line
    const membership = await pool.query(\line
      `SELECT * FROM group_members WHERE group_id = $1 AND user_id = $2`,\line
      [groupId, req.userId]\line
    );\line
    if (membership.rows.length === 0) \{\line
      return res.status(403).json(\{ message: 'You are not a member of this group.' \});\line
    \}\line
\line
    const \{ result, savedAttachment \} = await insertMessage(\line
      `INSERT INTO messages (content, user_id, group_id)\line
       VALUES ($1, $2, $3)\line
       RETURNING id, content, created_at`,\line
      [messageContent, req.userId, groupId],\line
      attachment\line
    );\line
\line
    const userResult = await pool.query('SELECT username FROM users WHERE id = $1', [req.userId]);\line
    const fullMessage = \{\line
      ...result.rows[0],\line
      attachment: savedAttachment,\line
      username: userResult.rows[0].username,\line
      user_id: req.userId,\line
      groupId: Number(groupId),\line
    \};\line
\line
    io.to(`group:$\{groupId\}`).emit('newGroupMessage', fullMessage);\line
\line
    res.status(201).json(fullMessage);\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Post group message error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
//fetching group messages\line
app.get('/api/groups/:groupId/messages', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  const \{ groupId \} = req.params;\line
  try \{\line
    const membership = await pool.query(\line
      `SELECT 1 FROM group_members WHERE group_id = $1 AND user_id = $2`,\line
      [groupId, req.userId]\line
    );\line
    if (membership.rows.length === 0) \{\line
      return res.status(403).json(\{ message: 'You are not a member of this group.' \});\line
    \}\line
\line
    await pool.query(\line
      `UPDATE messages\line
       SET read_at = NOW()\line
       WHERE group_id = $1\line
         AND user_id != $2\line
         AND read_at IS NULL`,\line
      [groupId, req.userId]\line
    );\line
\line
    const result = await pool.query(\line
      `SELECT \line
         m.id, m.content, m.created_at, m.edited_at, m.user_id, m.reply_to_id,\line
         u.username,\line
         r.content AS reply_content,\line
         ru.username AS reply_username,\line
         a.file_name AS attachment_name,\line
         a.mime_type AS attachment_mime_type,\line
         a.file_size AS attachment_file_size\line
       FROM messages m\line
       JOIN users u ON m.user_id = u.id\line
       LEFT JOIN messages r ON m.reply_to_id = r.id\line
       LEFT JOIN users ru ON r.user_id = ru.id\line
       LEFT JOIN message_attachments a ON a.message_id = m.id\line
       WHERE m.group_id = $1\line
       ORDER BY m.created_at ASC`,\line
      [groupId]\line
    );\line
    res.json(result.rows.map((row) => (\{ ...row, attachment: getAttachmentMetadata(row) \})));\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Get group messages error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
// Edit a group message \u8212? only the sender can edit their own\line
app.patch('/api/groups/messages/:messageId', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  const \{ messageId \} = req.params;\line
  const \{ content \} = req.body;\line
\line
  if (!content || !content.trim()) \{\line
    return res.status(400).json(\{ message: 'Message cannot be empty.' \});\line
  \}\line
\line
  try \{\line
    const result = await pool.query(\line
      `UPDATE messages\line
       SET content = $1, edited_at = NOW()\line
       WHERE id = $2 AND user_id = $3\line
       RETURNING id, content, edited_at, group_id`,\line
      [content, messageId, req.userId]\line
    );\line
\line
    if (result.rows.length === 0) \{\line
      return res.status(403).json(\{ message: 'You can only edit your own messages.' \});\line
    \}\line
\line
    const updated = result.rows[0];\line
    io.to(`group:$\{updated.group_id\}`).emit('groupMessageEdited', updated);\line
\line
    res.json(updated);\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Edit group message error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
\line
// Delete a group message \u8212? only the sender can delete their own\line
app.delete('/api/groups/messages/:messageId', authMiddleware, async (req, res) => \{\line
  const \{ messageId \} = req.params;\line
\line
  try \{\line
    const result = await pool.query(\line
      `DELETE FROM messages WHERE id = $1 AND user_id = $2 RETURNING id, group_id`,\line
      [messageId, req.userId]\line
    );\line
\line
    if (result.rows.length === 0) \{\line
      return res.status(403).json(\{ message: 'You can only delete your own messages.' \});\line
    \}\line
\line
    const deleted = result.rows[0];\line
    io.to(`group:$\{deleted.group_id\}`).emit('groupMessageDeleted', \{\line
      id: deleted.id,\line
      groupId: deleted.group_id,\line
    \});\line
\line
    res.status(200).json(\{ message: 'Message deleted.' \});\line
  \} catch (err) \{\line
    console.error('Delete group message error:', err);\line
    res.status(500).json(\{ message: 'Internal server error.' \});\line
  \}\line
\});\line
